@startuml frontend_product_boundary
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue (current debug console shell) and frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts (useRuntimeApi, BASE_PATH).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeSessionController.java.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java.
' Observed behavior: the current browser client calls the internal Runtime V1 contract directly and exposes credentials and protocol fields.
' Design reason: the product UI must use a public bridge so internal session identifiers, credentials, ETags, and raw SSE payloads do not cross the browser boundary.

title CampusClaw product frontend boundary
left to right direction

actor "Campus user" as User
rectangle "Product frontend" as Frontend {
  component "Agent and chat workspace" as Workspace
  component "Product event projector" as Projector
  component "Developer diagnostics\n(internal build only)" as Diagnostics
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Public chat API" as PublicApi
  component "Chat to session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Auth, policy, and event projection" as Policy
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "Session controllers" as Sessions
  component "Request-scoped SSE" as Stream
}

User --> Workspace : chat tasks
Workspace --> PublicApi : public HTTP and SSE
PublicApi --> Policy
Policy --> Mapping
Mapping --> Sessions : internal HTTP
Stream --> Policy : internal SSE events
Policy --> Projector : public safe events
Diagnostics ..> Sessions : local diagnostics only

note bottom of Frontend
Product constraints:
- No Service URL or credential editor
- No raw session_id, ETag, JSON, or SSE frames
- Agent, chat, and attachment metadata use public resources
end note

note bottom of Mate
Security hardening:
- Terminate browser authentication
- Authorize each action
- Project internal errors and events
- Do not byte-forward internal SSE
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Observed internal contract:
- 11 Session Runtime operations
- One active execution per Session
- Persistent Entry history plus transient progress events
end note
@enduml

@startuml assistant_rich_text_rendering
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java bde123706305a41e51c9a47b22e6ad11bbd8204c.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue lines 37-49 (assistant text interpolation).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts lines 40-55 (projectAssistantEvent) and 133-145 (text extraction).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/style.css lines 784-789 (.assistant-message plain pre-wrap styling).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java lines 149-176 and 215-238.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java lines 67-88, 195-210, 430-442, and 557-601.
' Observed behavior: assistant text is preserved across delta, completed entry, SSE, and history but the current Vue component renders it as plain text.
' Target-only design: the Markdown parser, safe AST policy, Vue rich-text components, and rendering budget are not implemented at this baseline.
' Security hardening: raw HTML, remote Markdown images, relative application routes, and dangerous URL schemes never become active DOM.
' Design reason: use one raw Markdown source and one renderer so streaming, completion, and history recovery converge to equivalent UI.

title Assistant safe rich-text rendering
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Runtime and public event input" as Input {
  component "assistant.message.delta\ntext fragment" as Delta
  component "assistant.message.completed\nfull persistent text" as Completed
  component "GET history\nfull persistent text" as History
}

rectangle "Conversation projection" as Projection {
  component "Assistant turn\nrawMarkdown and state" as Raw
  component "Stable block boundary\nplus escaped streaming tail" as Stable
}

rectangle "Safe rich-text renderer" as Renderer {
  component "Markdown parser\nraw HTML disabled" as Parser
  component "AST allowlist\nURL policy and render budget" as Policy
  component "Fixed Vue components\nno v-html or innerHTML" as Vue
}

rectangle "Assistant message UI" as UI {
  component "Paragraphs, headings,\nlists, and quotes" as Prose
  component "Scrollable semantic table" as Table
  component "Inline code and code block\nwith text-only copy" as Code
  component "Safe external link" as Link
  component "Escaped plain-text fallback" as Fallback
}

Delta --> Raw : append source text
Completed --> Raw : replace preview with authority
History --> Raw : restore the same source text
Raw --> Stable : throttle while streaming
Stable --> Parser : stable blocks and safe tail
Parser --> Policy : Markdown AST
Policy --> Vue : allowed nodes and attributes
Policy --> Fallback : rejected or over budget
Vue --> Prose
Vue --> Table
Vue --> Code
Vue --> Link

note bottom of Input
Observed source contract:
- Runtime carries text, not HTML
- completed and history are authoritative
- tool result and thinking use separate UI paths
end note

note bottom of Renderer
Security rules:
- Escape raw HTML
- Allow only absolute HTTP and HTTPS links
- Block Markdown image network requests
- Clamp heading levels inside the message
- Preserve source text for fallback and copy
end note

note bottom of UI
Responsive behavior:
- Only table and code containers scroll horizontally
- The page and composer never gain horizontal overflow
- Screen readers are notified once on completion
end note
@enduml

@startuml runtime_event_ui_projection
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java bde123706305a41e51c9a47b22e6ad11bbd8204c.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue lines 37-65 (thinking disclosure and result-only activity card).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts lines 40-90 and 112-145 (assistant, thinking, and result-only tool projection).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/types/product.ts lines 22-37 (AssistantTurn and ActivityTurn without arguments).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java lines 149-213 and 257-285.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java lines 67-88, 430-442, 512-517, and 557-601.
' Product-reference evidence: ChatGPT.app webview/assets/app-initial-BCLYDefw.js (followUpQueueMode, K9s) and webview/assets/zh-CN-ByRVSIXt.js.
' Observed behavior: thinking is attached to the assistant body; the frontend activity card shows result only; tool lifecycle events omit arguments, while assistant completed content preserves tool_call arguments.
' Target-only design: a chronological activity group and safe argument viewer are not implemented at this baseline.
' Security hardening: the public bridge redacts, maps, and budgets arguments before the browser renders inert structured text.
' Observed Codex behavior: desktop follow-up mode defaults to steer; a modifier submits one message with the inverse mode.
' Design reason: correlate ToolCallSpec, lifecycle, and result by toolCallId so thinking context and real tool inputs stay readable without exposing raw protocol data.

title Runtime events to product UI projection
left to right direction

rectangle "Runtime event families" as Events {
  component "user.message" as UserEvent
  component "assistant.message.started\nassistant.message.delta\nassistant.message.completed" as AssistantEvents
  component "assistant.thinking.started\nassistant.thinking.delta\nassistant.thinking.completed" as ThinkingEvents
  component "assistant completed\ntool_call name and arguments" as ToolSpec
  component "tool.execution.started\ntool.execution.completed\ntool.result" as ToolEvents
  component "session.status.idle\nstream.end\nstream.error" as TerminalEvents
}

rectangle "Frontend projection" as Projection {
  component "User turn" as UserTurn
  component "Streaming assistant turn" as AssistantTurn
  rectangle "Chronological Agent activity group" as ActivityGroup {
    component "Thinking row\nplain text disclosure" as ThinkingRow
    component "Expandable tool card\ninput before output" as ActivityCard
    component "Safe argument viewer\ninert key-value tree" as ArgumentViewer
  }
  component "Session and composer state" as SessionState
}

rectangle "User controls while running" as Controls {
  component "Adjust direction\n(default)" as Adjust
  component "Queue follow-up\n(configured or one-shot inverse)" as Continue
  component "Stop" as Stop
}

UserEvent --> UserTurn : persist and render
AssistantEvents --> AssistantTurn : preview then replace with final
ThinkingEvents --> ThinkingRow : stream then persist full text
ToolSpec --> ActivityCard : correlate by toolCallId
ToolEvents --> ActivityCard : merge lifecycle and result
ActivityCard --> ArgumentViewer : render safe arguments
TerminalEvents --> SessionState : idle, complete, or recoverable error

Adjust --> SessionState : internal steer
Continue --> SessionState : internal follow-up
Stop --> SessionState : internal abort

note bottom of ActivityCard
Running and failed tools stay expanded.
Successful tools may collapse after the final answer.
Input appears before output in the same card.
No second card is created for late metadata.
end note

note bottom of ArgumentViewer
Public bridge duties:
- redact sensitive values
- map internal paths and resource IDs
- clamp depth, length, and collection size
- never activate HTML, Markdown, or URLs
end note

note bottom of SessionState
Network loss does not replay the POST.
Reload persistent history and deduplicate
by the public event identity.

Adjust direction does not interrupt the
current model call or tool execution.
end note
@enduml
